Modifications from upstream
---------------------------

Only mechanical edits, no behavioural changes to grading or harness
orchestration:

  1. Absolute imports rewritten to relative — every ``from src.foo``
     became ``from .foo`` because the tree is now a Python subpackage
     under ``evals.third_party.swt_bench`` rather than upstream's
     top-level ``src``.

  2. ``__init__.py`` opens with
       from evals.common.docker_ssh import apply_ssh_patch
       apply_ssh_patch()
     so the harness can reach a remote Docker daemon via
     ``DOCKER_HOST=ssh://…`` on a macOS dev box without requiring
     paramiko to read the Keychain. See
     ``evals/sandboxes/docker_ssh.py`` for the full rationale.

Resync procedure
----------------

To pull a newer upstream:

  git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/logic-star-ai/swt-bench \\
      /tmp/swt-bench-upstream
  rsync -av --delete \\
      --include='*/' --include='*.py' --include='*.txt' --include='*.md' \\
      --exclude='*' \\
      /tmp/swt-bench-upstream/src/ evals/third_party/swt_bench/
  cp /tmp/swt-bench-upstream/LICENSE evals/third_party/swt_bench/
  # Re-run the import rewrite (see git log for the helper) and re-add
  # the apply_ssh_patch() prelude to __init__.py.

Reference: ReProAgent (https://github.com/iSEngLab/ReProAgent) does the
same vendor pattern under ``src/swtbench/`` — verified verbatim copy
plus relative-import rewrite, no other deltas.
